      "id": "serialization-factory",
      "name": "SerializationFactory",
      "category": "ImplicitObject",
      "signature": "SerializationFactory(Ar, Obj)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Ar",
          "type": "FChaosArchive&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Obj",
          "type": "FImplicitObject*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "FImplicitObject*",
      "docs": "Base class for implicit collision geometry such as spheres, capsules, boxes, etc.\nSome shapes are represented by a core shape with a margin. E.g. Spheres are\na point with a margin equal to the radius; boxes are a core AABB with a margin.\nThe margin is considered to be physically part of the shape for the pupose\nof collision detection, separating distance, etc.\nThe margin exists to make GJK and EPA collision more robust, and is not required\nby all derived types. E.g., We never use GJK to perform triangle-triangle collision\nso we do not need a margin on triangles. We would need a margin on every type\nthat can be tested against a triangle though."
    },
